  "slug": "spatial-transcriptomics-6c8f",
  "summary": "Integrating proteomics, glycoproteomics and transcriptomics across cohorts now exposes molecular links to ovarian and pancreatic cancer.",
  "synthesis": "The five preprints share an emphasis on integrating multiple molecular layers to define tumor regulatory states. Matched serum proteomics and intact N-glycoproteomics of 100 participants, analysed with a new differential-trend-subtype (DTS) framework, link glycan remodelling to ovarian cancer. In pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma, PDAC BioPortal unifies bulk, single-nucleus and spatial transcriptomic cohorts, while spatial transcriptomics of CA19-9-positive regions yields four transcriptional programs associated with survival and cell-line drug sensitivity. PTMlink scores glycosylation–phosphorylation co-variation across 1,211 tumor proteomes, and PathwayTheme reverses the usual PCA workflow by decomposing per-sample pathway scores to test pathway-level axes of variation. The common thread is methodological and resource-oriented: cross-layer co-variation and pathway-level axes are made testable rather than inferred from single modalities.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
